Number literals you pick with Code Selector are placed
on the data stack when executed.

DUSTY-12 uses the data stack as a staging area for values.
Most instructions are going to take some values from the data stack
and then place back the results instead.

It is nice to inspect the content of the data stack
any moment in time.
The telemetry stream from the data stack inspector allows
you to do just that. It would be invaluable to have
observability into the DUSTY-12 stack for the following
experiments, so HQ is requesting to set it up.

Enable telemetry on dataline 7 to be able to inspect the data stack
values.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
Use OBUS instruction to open data lines,
place a line number on stack first:
    07
    OBUS
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
07
OBUS -- enable the data stack telemetry

